<h1>GitHub Action</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Add Gate to your CI pipeline with the official GitHub Action. Scan pull requests, upload SARIF results, and get Slack notifications.</p>

    <h2 id="installation">Installation</h2>

    <p>Add Gate to any GitHub Actions workflow. The action (a Node 24 action, <code>uses: penumbraforge/gate@v2</code>) installs Gate, runs a full scan of the checked-out repository, and reports results.</p>

    <div class="gh-action">
      <div class="gh-action-bar">.github/workflows/gate.yml</div>
      <div class="gh-action-body"><span class="kw">name</span>: Gate
<span class="kw">on</span>: [pull_request, push]

<span class="kw">jobs</span>:
  <span class="kw">scan</span>:
    <span class="kw">runs-on</span>: ubuntu-latest
    <span class="kw">steps</span>:
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: actions/checkout@v4
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: penumbraforge/gate@v2
        <span class="kw">with</span>:
          <span class="kw">mode</span>: enforce
          <span class="kw">verify</span>: <span class="val">true</span>
          <span class="kw">format</span>: sarif
          <span class="kw">fail-on</span>: high</div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="inputs">All Inputs</h2>

    <table class="cmd-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>mode</td><td>report</td><td><code>enforce</code> fails the workflow on findings. <code>report</code> (the default) just logs them.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>verify</td><td>false</td><td>Check if detected credentials are active via provider APIs (opt-in).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>format</td><td>text</td><td>Output format: <code>text</code>, <code>json</code>, or <code>sarif</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>fail-on</td><td>high</td><td>Minimum severity to fail the workflow: <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code>, <code>high</code>, <code>critical</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>failure-mode</td><td>(from mode)</td><td>How findings or scan errors are treated: <code>block</code> or <code>warn</code>. Defaults to <code>block</code> when <code>mode: enforce</code>, otherwise <code>warn</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>slack-webhook</td><td>(none)</td><td>Slack incoming webhook URL for notifications. Use a GitHub secret.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>github-token</td><td>github.token</td><td>GitHub token for PR comments and SARIF upload. The default token works for most cases.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>use-local</td><td>false</td><td>Run the checked-out repo's own CLI (<code>node bin/gate.js</code>) instead of installing <code>@penumbraforge/gate</code> from npm. For self-testing unreleased versions.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="outputs">All Outputs</h2>

    <table class="cmd-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Output</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>findings-count</td><td>Number of findings at or above the <code>fail-on</code> severity (integer).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>blocked</td><td><code>true</code> if the action blocked the workflow (findings present and failure mode is <code>block</code>).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>scan-report</td><td>The JSON scan report itself (findings are capped so the output stays under GitHub's 1&nbsp;MiB output limit). Secrets are never included — matches are redacted and each finding carries a <code>secretHash</code>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="sarif-upload">SARIF Upload for Code Scanning</h2>

    <p>When <code>format</code> is set to <code>sarif</code>, the action runs a second scan in SARIF 2.1.0 format and uploads the result directly to GitHub Code Scanning — no separate upload step needed. Findings appear as code scanning alerts in the Security tab.</p>

    <div class="gh-action">
      <div class="gh-action-bar">.github/workflows/gate.yml</div>
      <div class="gh-action-body"><span class="kw">name</span>: Gate
<span class="kw">on</span>: [pull_request, push]

<span class="kw">permissions</span>:
  <span class="kw">security-events</span>: write   <span class="cmt"># required for SARIF upload</span>
  <span class="kw">contents</span>: read

<span class="kw">jobs</span>:
  <span class="kw">scan</span>:
    <span class="kw">runs-on</span>: ubuntu-latest
    <span class="kw">steps</span>:
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: actions/checkout@v4

      - <span class="kw">name</span>: Run Gate
        <span class="kw">id</span>: gate
        <span class="kw">uses</span>: penumbraforge/gate@v2
        <span class="kw">with</span>:
          <span class="kw">mode</span>: enforce
          <span class="kw">format</span>: sarif
          <span class="kw">fail-on</span>: high</div>
    </div>

    <div class="info-box">
      <strong>Note:</strong> SARIF upload requires the <code>security-events: write</code> permission and a <code>github-token</code> (the default token works). If the upload fails, the action logs a warning rather than failing the workflow.
    </div>

    <h2 id="pr-comments">PR Comments</h2>

    <p>When running on a <code>pull_request</code> event with findings at or above the threshold, the action automatically adds a comment to the PR summarizing the scan results. The comment includes:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Total finding count, with critical and high counts broken out</li>
      <li>A table of file locations, line numbers, rule names, and severities (first 25 findings)</li>
      <li>Suggested next steps (<code>gate fix</code>, <code>gate scan --interactive</code>)</li>
    </ul>

    <p>PR comments require the default <code>github-token</code> (provided automatically) or a token with <code>pull-requests: write</code> permission.</p>

    <h2 id="slack">Slack Notifications</h2>

    <p>Send scan results to a Slack channel using an incoming webhook. Store the webhook URL as a GitHub secret.</p>

    <div class="gh-action">
      <div class="gh-action-bar">.github/workflows/gate.yml</div>
      <div class="gh-action-body"><span class="kw">name</span>: Gate
<span class="kw">on</span>: [push]

<span class="kw">jobs</span>:
  <span class="kw">scan</span>:
    <span class="kw">runs-on</span>: ubuntu-latest
    <span class="kw">steps</span>:
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: actions/checkout@v4
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: penumbraforge/gate@v2
        <span class="kw">with</span>:
          <span class="kw">mode</span>: audit
          <span class="kw">verify</span>: <span class="val">true</span>
          <span class="kw">slack-webhook</span>: {% raw %}${{ secrets.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL }}{% endraw %}</div>
    </div>

    <p>The Slack message includes a summary of findings with severity counts and a link to the workflow run.</p>

    <h2 id="examples">Example Workflows</h2>

    <h3>Basic scan</h3>
    <p>The simplest workflow. Scans on every push and pull request, fails on any finding.</p>

    <div class="gh-action">
      <div class="gh-action-bar">basic</div>
      <div class="gh-action-body"><span class="kw">name</span>: Gate
<span class="kw">on</span>: [pull_request, push]

<span class="kw">jobs</span>:
  <span class="kw">scan</span>:
    <span class="kw">runs-on</span>: ubuntu-latest
    <span class="kw">steps</span>:
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: actions/checkout@v4
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: penumbraforge/gate@v2</div>
    </div>

    <h3>Full workflow</h3>
    <p>Verification, SARIF upload, PR comments, and Slack notifications.</p>

    <div class="gh-action">
      <div class="gh-action-bar">full</div>
      <div class="gh-action-body"><span class="kw">name</span>: Gate Security Scan
<span class="kw">on</span>:
  <span class="kw">pull_request</span>:
    <span class="kw">branches</span>: [main]
  <span class="kw">push</span>:
    <span class="kw">branches</span>: [main]

<span class="kw">permissions</span>:
  <span class="kw">security-events</span>: write
  <span class="kw">contents</span>: read
  <span class="kw">pull-requests</span>: write

<span class="kw">jobs</span>:
  <span class="kw">scan</span>:
    <span class="kw">runs-on</span>: ubuntu-latest
    <span class="kw">steps</span>:
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: actions/checkout@v4
        <span class="kw">with</span>:
          <span class="kw">fetch-depth</span>: 0   <span class="cmt"># full history for git scanning</span>

      - <span class="kw">name</span>: Run Gate
        <span class="kw">id</span>: gate
        <span class="kw">uses</span>: penumbraforge/gate@v2
        <span class="kw">with</span>:
          <span class="kw">mode</span>: enforce
          <span class="kw">verify</span>: <span class="val">true</span>
          <span class="kw">format</span>: sarif
          <span class="kw">fail-on</span>: high
          <span class="kw">slack-webhook</span>: {% raw %}${{ secrets.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL }}{% endraw %}</div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="using-outputs">Using Outputs in Subsequent Steps</h2>

    <p>Access Gate outputs in later workflow steps:</p>

    <div class="code-block"><span class="dim">- name: Check results</span>
  <span class="kw">if</span>: steps.gate.outputs.blocked == 'true'
  <span class="kw">run</span>: |
    echo "Gate found {% raw %}${{ steps.gate.outputs.findings-count }}{% endraw %} findings"
    echo '{% raw %}${{ steps.gate.outputs.scan-report }}{% endraw %}' > gate-report.json</div>
